course: dictionary
lesson: 8321
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so you must use the sentence to choose the right one. «The Great Sphinx is carved from the rock next to the pyramids.» Here rock is the hard, solid material that the Earth is made of, not a sweet or a kind of music.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. A rock pool is a pool of water left among rocks at the shore, so the sentence about sharks tells you rock is part of the place, not a thing you can sit on. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Rock can also be a verb, which is an action. «Some leaf insects rock gently like a leaf in the breeze.» Here rock means to move gently from side to side. Compare it with «The earthquake rocked the town», where rock means to shake or shock.
fact: Rock can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action), so check what job it does in the sentence.
fact: A rock is a large stone, and the hard material the Earth's surface is made of is also called rock.
fact: There are three kinds of rock: igneous, from cooled lava; sedimentary, layers pressed together that may hold fossils; and metamorphic, changed by heat and pressure.
fact: «A fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks can slip.»
fact: Rock can also mean a hard sweet on a stick, a loud style of music with guitars and drums, or, in «rock bottom», the lowest point.
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is carved from the rock next to the pyramids.» What does rock mean here? | A hard sweet on a stick | To move gently from side to side | A kind of loud music | *The hard, solid material of the Earth
exercise: «The earthquake rocked the town.» What does rocked mean? | Sang loudly | Sat down quietly | Moved gently like a cradle | *Shook or shocked
exercise: «Sitting on a rock by the sea.» What does rock mean in this sentence? | To shake | A hard sweet | A kind of music | *A large stone
test: «Some leaf insects rock gently like a leaf in the breeze.» What does rock mean here? | A large stone | Loud music with guitars and drums | A hard sweet on a stick | *To move gently from side to side
test: «A fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks can slip.» Which kind of rock is formed when layers are pressed together? | Igneous | Soil | Metamorphic | *Sedimentary
exam: Which sentence uses rock as a verb meaning to move gently back and forth? | «Rock bottom is the lowest point.» | *«Rock the baby until she sleeps.» | «Sitting on a rock by the sea.» | «Rock music is loud.»
